#resource "\\Files\\Icons\\bk_ddw.bmp"

//--- R-PANELUI2 (2026-09-11): every remaining panel bitmap. The redesign
//--- draws its chrome from pre-rendered BMPs (MT4 cannot blur, gradient or
//--- round a corner at runtime), so each one MUST be embedded here — an
//--- undeclared bitmap fails silently and the row renders as bare labels.
//--- P-UI-06: one runtime bitmap = one #resource. Generated by
//--- tools/gen-th3-icons.js; list maintained by tools/add-panel-resources.py.
//--- card skins, icon chips, switches, rails, washes and pills
//--- the wide card's COMPOSED body (P-UI-71c). `pnl_cardW{n}` stops at 12
//--- pair-lines while card 2 needs 13 and the Base Box card 19, so a wide body
//--- is built from these four pieces (top cap + one band per pair-line + the
//--- footer cap + the `.fade` wash — tools/slice-card-skins.py). A piece that is
//--- sliced but NOT declared here compiles clean and renders as NO CARD AT ALL:
//--- that is exactly what shipped (the user's "پشت پس زمینه نداره"), so
//--- `tools/panel-wiring-audit.py` now fails the build when a runtime
//--- `::Files\\Icons\\*.bmp` reference has no declaration (its [chrome] check).
#resource "\\Files\\Icons\\pnl_cardWbot.bmp"
#resource "\\Files\\Icons\\pnl_cardWfade.bmp"
#resource "\\Files\\Icons\\pnl_cardWmid.bmp"
#resource "\\Files\\Icons\\pnl_cardWtop.bmp"

//--- R-PANELUI2 (2026-09-11): every remaining panel bitmap. The redesign
//--- draws its chrome from pre-rendered BMPs (MT4 cannot blur, gradient or
//--- round a corner at runtime), so each one MUST be embedded here — an
//--- undeclared bitmap fails silently and the row renders as bare labels.
//--- P-UI-06: one runtime bitmap = one #resource. Generated by
//--- tools/gen-th3-icons.js; list maintained by tools/add-panel-resources.py.
//--- card skins, icon chips, switches, rails, washes and pills
// ICON-DIET 2026-09-27: pnl_cardW1..12 (+f) are 25.4 MB and produced by nothing.
// The wide card body is COMPOSED (P-UI-71c) from the four pieces below; this
// whole baked family was the pre-P-UI-71 lookup table. Deleting it is the
// single largest byte win in the repo and costs no runtime path.
// (PNL_WIDE_ROWS_MAX, the constant that named this range, is gone too.)
//--- P-DRAW-73: `pnl_hairW_gold` and `pnl_topbarW_gold` moved DOWN to DrawStrip.mqh,
//--- the only module with a runtime path for them (the wide gear head). They were
//--- declared here, so a wide panel's head art depended on this file being included
//--- in the same compilation unit (F-03: a workaround is named where it is used).
#resource "\\Files\\Icons\\pnl_secbandW.bmp"

